<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73866" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμό-τονος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>having the same tension,
				with equal force,</i> of fevers, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				10.615
			</span></i> ; <i>having equal muscular power in every muscle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Gym.</u>
				36
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως,</span> of the pulse, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				9.84
			</span></i> ; of traction, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				13.685
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>having the same pitch,</i> in Music, <i><span class="en">
				Nicom.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				11.5
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ λεγόμενα ὁ.</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σημεῖα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Gaud.Harm.
				21
			</span></i> : neut. sg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ., τό,</span> between <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαρύ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				17c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>equable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὁμαλὲς καὶ ὁ. ἐν τῇ τιμῇ τῆς
					φιλοσοφίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					1.14
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				36.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως</span>
			<i>uniformly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φερομένου τοῦ ἡλίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					911a14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>having the same accent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				75.16
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				11
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως, τινι</span> St.Byz.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παραισός.</span>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
